    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG are delighted to present number 47 Fassaugh Avenue.Moderisation is required on this two-bed property which offers a lovely light-filled home in a very popular location. There is a large front garden with off street parking.There is a side entrance which links to a good sized walled back garden.This location with great transport links is within walking distance to the Luas line and frequent bus links. This property is less than 15 minutes from the city centre by car. The location offers access to The Phoenix Park, The shops and restaurants of Phibsboro and TUD Grangegorman is 5-10 minutes by car.The accommodation comprises of: porch,an entrance hall, hallway,sitting room, separate kitchen/dining area. Upstairs there are two good-sized bedrooms and a bathroom.Viewing is highly recommended.Viewing is by appointment with the DNG Phibsboro office. Please contact DNG on 01 8300989 Negotiators: Brian McGee MIPAV, Ciarán Jones and Vincent Mullen MIPAV, Isabel O`Neill,Isabel O`Neill, Leah Barry and Michelle Keeley MIPAV are handling the sale."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nPorch - 1.77m x 0.45m\nPorch with good light and tiled floor.\n\nEntrance Hall - 2.74m x 1.76m\nEntrance hall, gives access to living room and kitchen.\n\nSitting Room - 3.08m x 2.76m\nSitting faces onto front garden with good light.\n\nKitchen Dining Room - 4.8m x 3.39m\nSpacious kitchen/dining room with access to back garden.There is understairs storage.\n\nLanding - 1.46m x 0.9m\nLanding area with good light.\n\nBedroom 1 - 3.4m x 3.9m\nDouble bedroom located at the front of the house with wooden flooring.\n\nBedroom 2 - 3.2m x 2.86m\nBedroom located at the back of the house with wooden flooring.\n\nBathroom - 1.84m x 1.4m\nBedroom with shower,W/C, W.H.B. There is a window for light and ventilation.\n\nOutside - \nThere is a front garden with off-street parking.There is a side entrance with access to the back garden.There is a back garden which is walled.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Negotiator",
        "SortOrder": 10,
        "Content": "Brian McGee"
      }
    ],
